sequenceDiagram
    participant Agent as claude agent
    participant HL as hooklistener (127.0.0.1:ephemeral)
    participant App as app.App (backend)
    participant FE as Frontend (Svelte)
    participant User as User

    Note over Agent,HL: hook config (URL + Bearer token) written to .claude/settings.json by ClaudeMonitor

    Agent->>HL: POST PreToolUse (Bearer token), blocks until a verdict
    HL->>App: agent:event (approval, reqID)
    App->>FE: agent:event (ApprovalCard)
    FE->>User: show Allow / Always / Deny

    User->>FE: click Allow
    FE->>App: App.Approve(reqID, "allow")
    App->>HL: Monitor.Approve → hooklistener.Decide(reqID, allow)
    HL-->>Agent: permissionDecision allow (unblocks the POST)
    Agent->>Agent: continues the tool call

    Note over Agent,HL: lifecycle hooks (SessionStart / Stop / StopFailure) POST non-blocking
    Agent->>HL: POST lifecycle event
    HL->>App: agent:event (state: running / idle / done / errored)
    App->>FE: agent:event → re-render state glyph

    Note over Agent,User: AskUserQuestion (opencode question.asked) is an attention SIGNAL, not an approval
    Agent->>HL: POST PreToolUse AskUserQuestion
    HL->>HL: auto-allow immediately, never blocks. ExitPlanMode stays on the approval path
    HL->>App: agent:event (kind question, state awaiting-input)
    App->>FE: agent:event → sidebar "asking you" feel, cyan pulse. User answers in the agent's own pane TUI

    Note over App,FE: opencode lifecycle events arrive over the opencode serve SSE /event stream. The approval loop above is Claude's ALONE
    Note over App,User: opencode permission.asked is a passive SIGNAL like a question: caps.approvals=false, no card, no Approval payload, no reply. opencode's attach TUI owns the prompt; perch only lights the sidebar awaiting-approval feel + blocking notification
